Z||000000||gtsonly||01-14-2001||09:19 AM||||What is the Wierdest or Wildest thing you have ever found in a Fiero?<P> I was junkyard searching for Fiero goodies last summer and found this Fiero which had in it, One plastic egg for pantyhose, used condom packages and pages from a gay porn magazine. But the car did have a perfect condition radio cowling which I got for 3 bucks!!!!<BR>   <P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||6
Z||000001||LarryB||01-14-2001||10:30 AM||||About 2 years ago I came out of work and got inside my SC when I heard noises inside the front.  When I lifted the hood open to see WTF was going on a *rat* scurried out.  Startled the heck out of me. <P><BR>||||reg||4
Z||000002||87GT||01-14-2001||08:35 PM||||The other day, I went to a local junkyard that had 9 fieros there.  8 were 4 cyl fieros and only one was a V6 fiero.  I went over to the lone V6 fiero and opened the door to find a tan interior with Purple Crushed Velvet over the bottom door trim.  It was the ugliest thing I had ever seen.  The car was totally abused.  I guess thats why it was at a junkyard.  sigh...||||reg||1
Z||000003||80's BOY||01-14-2001||10:45 PM||||on my legally bought parts car, when i pulled the shifter and panels there were several marijuana joints stashed in the bottom. it was pretty funny.||||reg||6
Z||000004||KRMFiero||01-15-2001||10:03 AM||||Well its not a Fiero, My Friend Jay had me put a system in his VW he got,  when we took the front left spekeker grill out we notice there was no speaker, there was a huge zip lock bag and like a little bit of weed (not much but enough to know thats what his car was used for hehe)||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||01-15-2001||11:06 AM||||not in a Fiero either, but when I was working for a car dealership, we pulled a trade in car back to do some work and there were 2 grocery bags in trunk of 'grass' plants.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever2||01-15-2001||11:48 AM||||Three important things I've learned from the Forum:<BR>1)-Always carry a fire extinguisher<BR>2)-Always carry a camera<BR>3)-Check the car for dope before any police dogs come sniffing around.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||01-15-2001||12:36 PM||||8 mice nested and died in the heater motor, I removed the taillight and found another mice nest along with a dead garder snake , took 8 months to get the smell out of the car. NEVER STORE YOUR CAR IN A BARN! NO MATTER HOW CHEAP. Also found a set of keys taped to the bottom of the drivers seat, with 2" wide GM logo tape ..go figure. Now that we have built a new garage , my car has a nice dry place..in good company too , 2 corvairs and a vette.....<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
